-# create a range of source files, then fsr them to a known size
-#
-# This assumes 256 byte inodes.
-#
-# n =3D number of target fragments for xfs_fsr
-#=09- only a guideline, but forces multiple fragments via sync writes
-#=09- start at 4 as that typically covers all extent format situations
-#=09- end at 12 as that is beyond the maximum that canbe fit in extent
-#=09  format
-# i =3D number of 2 byte attributes on the file
-#=09- it takes 6 attributes to change the fork offset from the start v=
alue
-#=09  of 120 bytes to 112 bytes, so we start at 5.
-#=09- 15 is enough to push to btree format, so we stop there.
-# j =3D number of data extents on the file
-#=09- start in extent format, but we also want btree format as well, s=
o
-#=09  start at 5 so that the number of attributes determines the start=
ing
-#=09  format.
-#=09- need enough extents that if they are all 3 blocks in length the =
final
-#=09  format will be dependent on the number of attributes on the inod=
e. 20
-#=09  initial single block extents gives us 6-8 extents after defrag w=
hich
-#=09  puts us right on the threshold of what the extent format can hol=
d.
